{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30136 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Tigloylgomisin H appears to have a shared target of A2780cisR through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Tigloylgomisin H to VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, and the second pathway links Tigloylgomisin H to Raji, which is targeted by Ginsenoside Rs5. The third pathway connects Tigloylgomisin H to VMRC-LCP, which is also targeted by Cocosamide B. All three pathways ultimately converge on A2780cisR as a target. This suggests that Tigloylgomisin H may act through a common mechanism or a series of overlapping pathways that ultimately lead to the activation of A2780cisR. The evidence supports a potential role for Tigloylgomisin H in modulating A2780cisR through a network of targets, possibly involving the regulation of gene expression or signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, with A2780cisR potentially being a downstream effector of multiple molecular actors.",
